== Software and creator projects ==

=== VRCGT — VRChat Group Tools ===

[https://github.com/0xE69/VRCGT VRCGT] is an independent Windows desktop application for VRChat group owners and moderators, developed using C#, .NET and WPF.

The project's published documentation describes:

* Group information, member and role management.
* Moderation workflows and audit-log review.
* Group posts, calendar events and join requests.
* Discord webhook notifications.
* Member snapshots, role recovery and re-invitation workflows.
* Configurable monitoring of administrative activity.<ref name="vrcgt">[https://github.com/0xE69/VRCGT VRCGT — project README and documentation], GitHub.</ref>

The project aims to bring related administration tasks into a single interface. Available functionality depends on the version and the user's group permissions.

Status: Public source repository. Refer to the repository for documentation, builds and current functionality.

[https://github.com/0xE69/VRCGT Source code and documentation] · [https://github.com/0xE69/VRCGT/issues Issue tracker]

=== VR.API ===

VR.API is an independent experimental project exploring backend services and API integration for VRChat-related community tools.

Its focus includes administration workflows, service integration and automation that supports community operations.

The project is separate from VRChat's own services. Its name does not indicate an official API, partnership or endorsement.

Status: Development and experimentation.

=== VRC.STORE ===

[https://vrc.store VRC.STORE] is an independent marketplace project intended to support creators producing content for VRChat.

The planned scope includes multi-vendor distribution of avatars, avatar assets, world assets and creator tools.

The project remains in development. Proposed marketplace functionality should not be interpreted as an available service until it has been released.

Status: In development, with a provisional target of 2027. This is not a confirmed launch date.

[https://vrc.store Project website]

=== VR Creator Hub / VR HUB ===

VR Creator Hub, also referred to as VR HUB, is a creator-focused initiative centred on collaboration, technical discussion and shared VR projects.

Its focus includes connecting creators and community organisers, exchanging development knowledge and exploring tools that support collaborative work.

The initiative complements REΛLITY's wider interest in creator services and community infrastructure.

== VR tracking research ==

=== APVR / AirPose VR ===

APVR / AirPose VR is an independent hardware and software research project led by REΛLITY.

The project investigates full-body tracking without body-worn trackers, with intended applications in social VR, including VRChat.

Current work focuses on prototype development, tracking and calibration research, and exploring how the system could integrate with existing VR software.

The goal is to investigate a different approach to body tracking and understand its practical limitations through development and testing.

Status: Research and prototyping. Tracking performance, compatibility, product specifications and release timing remain subject to validation.

